Z||000000||Tigger||03-14-2001||12:03 AM||||Actually no, I just wanted to let everyone know I had spotted 3 Fieros today.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  All red, all 84 or 85 coupes.<P>One, dead on I-69 going home.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Nobody was around, so I didn't stop.  The second one was seen running deliveries for the local Little Caesar's.  And the third appears to be working at the new Burger King in town.<P>I seen all three at different times today so I'm not sure yet if all three were the same car.  I thinkin the one parked at Burger King is the same one working the pizza delivery, might be the same guy working two jobs.<P>The snow is almost gone here... anyone else seen any Fieros out and about lately?<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue3.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||rodmcneill||03-14-2001||12:26 AM||||I've seen a couple of 85 GT's running around town in South Bend. Of course I see mine every day(86GT) that has become my daily driver since my(ex) girlfriend threw a rod through the block of my 89 Grand Am turbo. I do enjoy the drive to work. Once the snow goes away for good I will have to visit my car wash and spray the underside really well. A clean Fiero is a happy Fiero!||||reg||10
Z||000002||Cheever2||03-14-2001||12:38 AM||||Tigger, I trust you left some Forum cards?<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||wahoo4u||03-14-2001||01:12 AM||||couldn't believe my eyes this past weekend.  Went to Davenport IA about a six hour trip one way.  Saw 11 count them 11 fieros total. Ranging from and 84 base coupe to a blue 87 GT to a yellow 88 formula.  Including, and I am not sure why,  a whole car transport full of fieros.  They all looked in good shape.  I wish I knew where they were going, I would have followed to see if I could take them off of there hands.  All in all a great weekend.  You can tell spring must be getting closer in Iowa, all the fieros are coming out of hiding.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||03-14-2001||07:36 AM||||wahoo,<P>Those were some CA Fieros from Fiero Dave's score late last year. 4 went to Milwaukee, WI and 3 to the central IN area. You are the only one who has made comment on seeing them!<BR>A bit strange since they traveled such a distance.<P>Copy and paste if necessary! Go here:<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=101570&a=12040235&f=null&vt=null" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=101570&a=12040235&f=null&vt=null</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||03-14-2001||07:49 AM||||Yes I have seen them too!  I am glad that the snow is going away.<P>There is an 85 GT that I pass every day to school and back that when it gets warmer and I get my Fiero running, I may stop and ask him if he still wants it.  It hasnt moved in a month at least, and is covered in leaves.  <P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
